WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:06.089
Hello, and welcome to the Epic Games training for Unreal Engine Tools, Source Control, and

2
00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:07.089
Collaboration.

3
00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:11.119
My name is Kevin Miller, and I'm an instructor for Epic Games.

4
00:00:11.119 --> 00:00:14.240
In this course, we'll start out by helping you with understanding Source Control's core

5
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.059
concepts and basic workflows.

6
00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:22.339
Then we'll look at server and client setup as we explore where to go and install Perforce.

7
00:00:22.339 --> 00:00:25.750
Then how to get your project into Perforce.

8
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.609
After that, we will briefly compare ShotGrid and Perforce as version control options

9
00:00:29.649 --> 00:00:34.289
before taking a look at how Epic Games utilizes ShotGrid in our production pipeline.

10
00:00:34.289 --> 00:00:40.109
Next, we'll look at version control inside Unreal Engine, and then explore Unreal Game

11
00:00:40.109 --> 00:00:43.909
Sync as an alternative to using the Perforce interface for project synchronization.

12
00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:48.640
We will also look at existing collaboration tools and see how it all comes together in

13
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.159
your production pipeline.

14
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:55.189
Finally, we will wrap up the course with a few final recommendations that cover organization,

15
00:00:55.189 --> 00:00:57.909
tips, and resources.

16
00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:02.549
Additionally, as you work through this course material, we will be providing a project file

17
00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:05.510
that you can upload to your own version control solution.

18
00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:12.390
The project file is the UET 216-06 demo, and it makes use of the Downtown West modular

19
00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:17.209
pack by Pure Polygons that can be found in the Epic Games Marketplace permanently

20
00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:18.920
free collection.

21
00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.579
Be sure to download that and add it to your library.

22
00:01:21.579 --> 00:01:26.489
Now, let's move on to our next section to help you understand Source Control.
